A step link, /flows/<flow id>?step=<id>, opens that flow with the drawer of the named step or branch already open, for example /flows/leafcutter/flow-render-pipeline?step=resolve, or the branch link /flows/fern-and-fig/checkout-and-pay?step=declined. The ?step= value is looked up among the flow's steps and branches, whose ids never collide within one flow, and at most one drawer opens. Everything else matches a canonical link: 200, the flow's own Source and Kind with Realization All, a breadcrumb showing only that flow, and the ?step= kept in the address bar. The drawer shows what the 'Open a step' step describes. Records: FlowRoute route-ac-drawer-link and route-ac-drawer-branch-link.

